{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nosy-drooly-milksnake","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`reconcile-check` exposes discrepancies, orphaned rebar/Jira bindings, unbound counts, checked/in-sync totals, formatting, exit behavior, and persisted report output. Its replacement cannot be guessed from command spelling: field-diff information belongs with preview, integrity/bindings with fsck, and operational witnesses with status.\n\n## Approach\n\nEnumerate each current observable and assign it to `bridge preview`, `bridge fsck`, or `bridge status`. Implement a new well-named bridge diagnostic subverb only if an observable does not coherently fit those owners. Migrate report persistence away from `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` while proving parity or recording explicit retirement for every field.\n\n## Scope\n\n- reconcile-check report construction and direct-engine output\n- bridge preview/fsck/status command/result contracts\n- persisted bridge-state reports, docs, and characterization tests\n\n## Testing\n\nUse characterization fixtures for healthy, discrepant, orphaned, and unbound state; compare fields, formatting, exits, and persistence before/after canonical bridge routing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every reconcile-check observable has a documented canonical bridge owner or an explicit approved retirement.\n- [ ] Preview exposes field-diff observations; fsck exposes binding/integrity diagnostics; status exposes operational witnesses.\n- [ ] Any new bridge diagnostic subverb has one coherent responsibility and a stable named result contract.\n- [ ] Persisted report behavior is migrated from `bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` with field/exit/format parity or explicit retirement evidence.\n- [ ] Characterization and canonical bridge tests cover healthy, discrepant, orphaned, and unbound cases.","id":"3b66-615c-fbfb-4b1f","parent_id":"0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","reconciler","bridge","migration"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Migrate reconcile-check diagnostics to canonical bridge operations"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788314404027786001,"uuid":"e04a45ee-e506-45af-bc5d-705dc07c4494"}